    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:styling-toggles-in-a-hierarchy:0015:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:styling-toggles-in-a-hierarchy:0015",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "For example, you can apply the `ToggleStyle/button` style to an `HStack`:",
      "normalizedSource": "For example, you can apply the `ToggleStyle/button` style to an `HStack`:",
      "sourceHash": "81c4932c382e8561d72155e3930b40ac868eccbe6fe86504a6aa171f1604fb43",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "You can set a style for all toggle instances within a view hierarchy by applying the style modifier to a container view.",
      "contextAfter": "```None\nHStack {\n    Toggle(isOn: $isFlagged) {\n        Label(\"Flag\", systemImage: \"flag.fill\")\n    }\n    Toggle(isOn: $isMuted) {\n        Label(\"Mute\", systemImage: \"speaker.slash.fill\")\n    }\n}\n.toggleStyle(.button)\n```",
      "documentTitle": "toggleStyle(:)",
      "framework": "PermissionKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
